# ==========================================================
# HEAVY DATA
# ==========================================================
*.parquet
*.npy
*.npz
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.h5

data/raw/*
!data/raw/atlas/
data/raw/atlas/*
# The Schaefer-400 fsaverage5 lookup is 21 KB and is the one input every Colab
# session needs before aggregate.py can run -- but `data/raw/` is gitignored, so
# a fresh clone never had it. Committing this single file removes a per-session
# copy step. It does not weaken §6.4 provenance: the atlas sha256 still travels
# inside every parcel table (docs/parcellation.md), and the `.annot` sources it
# was built from stay out of git (notebook 03 fetches them).
!data/raw/atlas/schaefer400_fsaverage5.npz

data/interim/*
!data/interim/units/
data/interim/units/*
!data/interim/units/be_001.json
data/processed/*
!data/processed/units.csv
# Phase III outputs. Both are already covered by the rules above (`*.parquet`
# globally, `data/processed/*` for the CSV), but they are named explicitly
# because they are the two largest things a Phase III run produces: at 5,000
# learners x 120 episodes x 3 conditions, responses.csv is ~5.4M rows. Neither is
# a source: both are rebuilt from the config hash + master seed recorded in the
# run log.
data/processed/*.parquet
data/processed/responses.csv
data/processed/learner_state.parquet

# `outputs/` is ignored wholesale, which already covers outputs/logs/. Named here
# so the Phase III run log -- config hash, seed, git commit, package versions,
# clip counts -- is visibly a per-run artifact rather than something that was
# forgotten.
outputs/
outputs/logs/
cache/
checkpoints/

# data/synthetic/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The placeholder units table is a
# few KB and committing it makes a development run reproducible from a clean
# clone. It is stamped `synthetic_placeholder` on every row, and no output
# derived from it is a project result (docs/phase3_assumptions.md §16).

# Phase II cache roots. Parcel tables and vertex arrays are build products of a
# GPU run; reproducibility comes from the pinned revision + config + cache keys,
# never from committing predictions. See docs/caching_policy.md.
data/interim/tribe_cache/
tribe_cache/
drive_local/

# ==========================================================
.env
.env.*
